 WORLD'S MOST POWERFUL SERVERS DELIVER UNPRECEDENTED DATABASE PERFORMANCE,
 Maynard, MA April 11'95 .... Digital and Oracle announced the computer
 industry's most powerful server/database systems.  The AlphaServer 8400
 enterprise server and AlphaServer 8200 departmental server, the first to
 use Digital's record-breaking BIPS (Billion Instructions Per Second) chip,
 deliver the industry's highest RISC performance and best price/performance
 for business-critical applications at one-tenth the price of the most
 widely used mainframes.  Complementing these servers, Oracle introduced
 64-bit technology that runs database applications up to 200 times faster
 than current 32-bit systems.  This is possible through the new Oracle Very
 Large Memory (Oracle VLM) capability of the Oracle7 database that allows a
 larger portion of the database to reside in memory, and exploits the 64-bit
 Alpha architecture, the Digital UNIX(R) operating system, and the 14GB
 maximum main memory of the new Digital Alpha 8400 and 8200 servers.

 * Digital Press Release - World's Most Powerful Servers/Database Deliver
   Unprecedented Performance; news0410.txt

 DIGITAL AND PROCESS SOFTWARE TO PROVIDE INDUSTRIAL-STRENGTH INTERNET WNT
 SERVERS .... On March 23, 1995, Digital announced a global distribution
 partnership making Digital a reseller of Purveyor (tm), Process Software's
 new World Wide Web (WWW) server software package for Windows NT.  This
 agreement benefits organizations looking for a powerful, cost-effective
 means of communicating in multimedia formats on the Internet using Alpha
 NT and Intel NT platforms.  WNT-based Internet servers are attractive
 because solutions are scalable and the need for higher performance does not
 increase the system management complexity or difficulty.  Purveyor allows
 corporations to publish public and confidential multimedia information
 on the Internet as well as on corporate local area networks.  Based on
 the widely-used public domain HTTP server from the European Microsoft
 Windows Academic Centre (EMWAC), commercial enhancements available through
 Process Software include advanced security features managed through a
 Microsoft Windows graphical user interface, support for HTTP, FTP and
 Gopher proxy servers, and full logging capabilities.

 * Press Release - Digital and Process Software to Provide Industrial-
   Strength Internet WNT Servers; news0401.txt

 DIGITAL INTRODUCES CONFIGURATION SWITCHES TO BUILD VIRTUAL LANS .... On
 March 27, 1995 Digital introduced two new port-level configuration switches
 that enable network managers to meet the increasing network performance
 demands of users and applications.  Combined with its DEChub 900 Multi-
 Switch architecture, the full family of high-performance LAN switches,
 and management software, Digital enables network managers to provide
 virtual LAN capabilities today.  Using the new products (PORTswitch 900
 family and latest version of HUBwatch management software) network managers
 can address the major issues facing high-performance networks: optimizing
 bandwidth to support powerful client/server and desktop applications;
 reducing time-intensive adds, moves, and changes; and ensuring a secure
 networking for workgroups and project teams.  The new products include:
 . PORTswitch 900TP - a 32-port, 10-BaseT configuration switch;
 . PORTswitch 900CP - a 16-port, 10-Base2 (Thinwire) configuration switch;
 . HUBwatch Ver 4.0 - low-cost Virtual LAN Management from a PC that manages
   the full DEChub product family, including the new PORTswitch family.

 * Digital Fact Sheets (2): PORTswitch 900 Family Fact Sheet and HUBwatch
   Virtual LAN Management System Fact Sheet;  news0402.txt

 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES EARLY ADOPTION OF INTEL'S POWERFUL PENTIUM 120MHz
 PROCESSOR .... On March 27, 1995 Digital Equipment Corporation announced
 that the new Intel 120MHz Pentium processor will be offered in Digital's
 Celebris family of desktop PCs.  The 120MHz Pentium processor is based on
 Intel's 3.3V processor, which was announced on the same day.  Specific
 configurations, delivery dates, and prices for the Intel 120MHz Pentium
 processor-based Celebris systems will be announced later this spring.
 According to Dataquest, the Digital Celebris XL systems are "at the top
 of the performance pile."  The Digital Celebris XL high-performance line
 was the first in the industry to fully exploit the processor independence
 features of the industry-standard PCI local bus, and the first PC system
 with a motherboard/daughtercard architecture that offers a CISC/RISC
 upgrade capability.  Since its introduction at the Fall COMDEX in 1993,
 the Celebris XL line continues to be highly rated in review after review.

 * Press Release - Digital Announces Early Adoption of Intel's Powerful
   Pentium 120MHz Processor; news0403.txt

 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES 1995 K-12 EDUCATION GRANT RECIPIENTS .... On March 28,
 1995, Digital Equipment Corporation announced the recipients of grants
 funded through Digital's New England-wide, K-12 Education Grant Program.
 The program, developed to promote academic excellence and enhance core
 competencies of students, provides cash grants to 19 schools in 14
 communities in Massachusetts, New Hampshire and Maine.  The grants
 support a variety of academic activities, ranging from teacher training
 and curriculum development to reading incentive and teen parenting
 programs.  Examples of funded programs include:
 . "Making Connections," an interdisciplinary curriculum integrating core
    academic subjects
 . "Environmental Learning Site," creates an outdoor lab for environmental
    studies
 . "Publishing Center," integrating writing and publishing skills into all
    aspects of a student's curriculum
 . "Playing With Math and Science," develops curriculum kits for
   independent study.

 * Press Release - Digital Announces 1995 K-12 Education Grant Recipients;
   news0404.txt

 INDUSTRY LEADERS CHOOSE DIGITAL SEMICONDUCTOR'S NETWORKING CHIPS,
 March 28, 1995 .... Apple Computer, Asante' Technologies, and Motorola
 Computer Group have expressed their intent to build computer products
 incorporating PCI Ethernet controller chips from Digital Semiconductor.
 Apple Computer has selected Digital Semiconductor's PCI-based 21040
 10Mbps (megabits per second) and 21140 10/100Mbps Ethernet controllers
 to develop network interface cards for the Macintosh and PC Windows
 environments.  Asante' Technologies will incorporate the 21140 Fast
 Ethernet chip in its Asante' FAST PCI Fast Ethernet implementation.
 Motorola Computer Group is using the 21040 PCI Ethernet controller
 in several motherboards and on a VME board.  Both the 21140 PCI Fast
 Ethernet and 21040 PCI Ethernet controllers act as PCI bus masters,
 featuring a direct memory access (DMA) architecture to optimize CPU
 utilization, and support full-duplex operation.  Both chips are supported
 with software drivers for all major operating system environments.

 * Press Release - Industry Leaders Choose Digital Semiconductor's
   Networking chips; news0405.txt

 SYNCSORT AVAILABLE FOR DIGITAL'S ALPHA SYSTEMS .... On March 29, 1995
 SyncSort, Inc. and Digital announced the availability of the high per-
 formance sort utility SyncSort on Digital Alpha systems running Digital
 UNIX (formerly OSF/1) and OpenVMS.  SyncSort recently showed record
 setting performance in benchmark tests by Digital on an AlphaServer 2100
 system with 25Gb of striped disk space, completing gigabyte sorts in
 less than 15 minutes and 100Mb sorts in less than a minute.  Organiza-
 tions migrating large applications from mainframes to UNIX need the same
 powerful tools on the UNIX platforms as they are accustomed to using on
 the mainframes.  SyncSort is the most frequently installed third-party
 software product on mainframe systems.

 FRAME TECHNOLOGY CORP. TO PORT PRODUCTS TO ALPHAGENERATION WORKSTATIONS
 AND SERVERS RUNNING DIGITAL UNIX, March 27, 1995 .... Frame Technology
 Corp. announced its intention to port FrameMaker, FrameViewer, and Frame
 Developer's Kit, release 5 products to AlphaGeneration workstations and
 servers running Digital UNIX.  Frame release 5 products will be available
 for Digital UNIX in Q4 1995.  In the interim, Frame will offer its
 Version 4 products running on Digital UNIX in early May.  Files created
 on the Digital Alpha workstations are fully compatible with FrameMaker
 files created on Macintosh, Windows and other UNIX platforms.  Frame
 software products and tools facilitate the complete document lifecycle,
 from creation and authoring, revisions and editing, tracking, and
 retrieval to electronic distribution and viewing.

 * Digital Press Release - Frame Technology Corp. To Port FrameMaker,
   FrameViewer, and Frame Developer's Kit To Alpha Workstations and
   Servers Running Digital UNIX; news0407.txt

 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES THE WORLD'S FASTEST WORKSTATION .... On April 3, 1995
 Digital unveiled the AlphaStation 250 4/266.  Priced at US$19,995 for a
 fully configured system, the new workstation meets the demanding needs of
 scientists and engineers in research, science, and technical markets and
 runs three operating systems: Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Microsoft's
 Windows NT.  With a clock rating of 266 MHz and SPECint92 and SPECfp92 of
 198.6 and 262.5 respectively, the AlphaStation 250 4/266 offers better
 performance and price/performance than competitor's workstations such as
 the HP 715 and 735, IBM's 3CT and 59H, Sun's SPARCstation, and Silicon
 Graphic's Indigo2 and PowerIndigo2.  The AlphaStation 250 4/266 is a
 channels-ready product, packaged with industry standard components such
 as the PCI bus, which enables a wide range of peripherals to be available
 from third parties.  The AlphaStation 250 4/266 comes with a three-year
 hardware warranty, featuring next-day response and onsite service for the
 first year.

 * Digital Fact Sheet - Digital Announces World's Fastest Workstation;
   news0408.txt

 NEW MULTIMEDIA PRODUCTS ENHANCE WORKSTATIONS, April 3, 1995 .... Digital
 further enhanced the multimedia capabilities of its AlphaStation work-
 stations with new features for Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX, and
 a new video capture and output card called FullVideo Supreme.  The new
 features provide users and developers with access to more industry stand-
 ard video formats, including MPEG-1 (widely used on the Internet) and
 Intel's Indeo (which enables the sharing of audio and video data with PCs).
 FullVideo Supreme allows users to develop and run multimedia applications
 that incorporate full-motion video, video clips, and stills when used in
 conjunction with Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX.  Multimedia
 Services for Digital UNIX is included free with every AlphaStation work-
 station running Digital UNIX; a developers license is priced at US$395.
 FullVideo Supreme is priced at US$895.  Both products are available now.

 * Digital Fact Sheets (2): Multimedia Services for Digital Unix Fact Sheet
   and FullVideo Supreme Video Card Fact Sheet; news0409.txt

