DIGITAL ANNOUNCES 1995 K-12 EDUCATION GRANT RECIPIENTS

Maynard, Mass., March 28, 1995 - Digital Equipment Corporation today
announced the recipients of grants funded through Digital's New
England-wide, K-12 Education Grant Program.

The program, developed to promote academic excellence and enhance core
competencies of students, provides a total of US$33,500 in cash grants
ranging from US$799 to US$2,500 to 19 schools in 14 communities in
Massachusetts, New Hampshire and Maine.

The grants will support a variety of academic activities, ranging
from teacher training and curriculum development to reading incentive
and teen parenting programs.  Examples of funded programs include:

o "Making Connections," an interdisciplinary curriculum integrating core
   academic subjects

o "Environmental Learning Site," which creates an outdoor lab for
   environmental studies

o "Publishing Center," integrating writing and publishing skills into all
   aspects of a student's curriculum

o "Playing With Math and Science," which develops curriculum kits for
   independent study.

According to Ann Hurd, Digital's New England Community and Government
Relations Manager, "Through the K-12 grant program, we are able to identify
and support creative teaching methods.  By providing teachers with
additional tools for the classroom, we have a direct impact on students and
their academic development."

The grants have been awarded to:

