with dithering and control of brightness, contrast, saturation, and image
sharpness without having to pay for features that they may not need.

The FullVideo Supreme video card can operate on any graphics subsystem,
which means that commodity as well as high-end 3D graphics options can be
used with it. Its analog video input allows for the use of cameras, VCRs,
and laser disks. Through its video output capabilities, users can record to
a VCR tape or play video back on a TV monitor. The video card provides
superb image quality for a given number of colors, dynamically maps video
to window size, and supports multiple video file formats and standard
connectors.

Multimedia--a combination of audio, video, text, graphics, and
animation--is a powerful method for presenting and manipulating
information. Digital's FullVideo Supreme video card helps users add a
critical component by allowing them to capture incoming video and
incorporate it into a wide range of applications for engineering, business,
education, and entertainment.

