AlphaServer 8400 5/300 Enterprise Server

HIGHLIGHTS

o  World's best performing, highest capacity, most reliable enterprise
   server at the best price

o  Capabilities beyond mainframe systems

o  Unsurpassed investment protection

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The first implementation of world's fastest microprocessor, the Alpha 21164,
has delivered the world's fastest enterprise server. The 64 bit Alpha
architecture has enabled the highest capacity enterprise server in the
industry -- the AlphaServer 8400 5/300. Taking advantage of advanced
technologies, Digital has created the most reliable and available
bet-your-business server there is. Couple this with the world's leading
applications, comprehensive enterprise server support infrastructure, and
users have a solution to solve the most demanding business problems at the
best price.

The AlphaServer 8400 5/300 is Digital's top-of-the-line enterprise server,
supporting up to 12 processors, 14 GB of memory, and 1.2 GB per second
(peak) of I/O. Because of a balanced system design and the fastest
processors available, the AlphaServer 8400 can deliver over 3,000
transactions per second and Linpack 1,000 x 1,000 of more than 2 GF
(gigaflops) in a single platform, making it the industry's best commercial
and technical server. Just like the DEC 7000 system, the AlphaServer 8400
supports OpenVMS, and Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) platforms. The DEC
7000 and VAX 7000 products can be upgraded to the AlphaServer 8400 in a few
hours, giving users unsurpassed performance today and the room to grow well
into the 21st century. The AlphaServer 8400 platform has been designed to
take full advantage of future generations of Alpha microprocessors, with
scalable performance.

The AlphaServer 8400 adds low cost, high performance PCI I/O to the
AlphaServer line, providing up to 144 PCI slots on 12 different physical PCI
buses. With over 1.2 GB per second of I/O, users can now build the largest
database servers with commodity components and have the reliability and
availability they've come to expect with expensive mainframes.

Each AlphaServer 8400 base system includes a 2 GB SCSI system disk,
in-cabinet CD-ROM reader, integrated I/O module with three FWD SCSI ports,
one single-ended SCSI port, two Ethernet ports, and one I/O hose port
on-board, plus optional connectivity for FDDI and Prestoserve daughter
cards. Each system also includes a choice of OpenVMS or Digital UNIX base
operating system licenses, a NAS 200 license, and a one-year hardware
warranty, which includes onsite, four-hour response, five-day-per-week
service.

BENEFITS

Users looking for alternatives to their expensive mainframes will find the
best business value with the AlphaServer 8400, its 64 bit architecture,
environment, and applications. The AlphaServer provides two times the
performance of today's mainframes at one-tenth the cost. Databases can now
take advantage of Alpha architectural features by holding huge (over 10 GB)
amounts of data in memory (also known as VLM or very large memory). This
translates into huge performance improvements for all applications.

Data Warehousing is a perfect example of an application that provides retail
(and many more) users with the ability to evaluate enormous amounts of
historic data in realtime, thus providing decision making support that sends
increased sales and profits straight to the bottom line year after year.
(See the "AlphaServer 8400 Delivers Mainframe Performance for Less Cost"
article in this issue.)

Another benefit of the AlphaServer 8400 is in the area of supercomputing.
High performance technical computing users now have a powerful, affordable
replacement or addition to their costly supercomputing environments. With a
peak of 7.2 GF, the AlphaServer 8400 allows more throughput, better
turnaround, and the ability to tackle larger more complex problems than ever
before. With the Alpha 64 bit architecture, there is no need to convert
existing 64 bit supercomputer applications. They move to the AlphaServer
8400 with ease. With a rich portfolio of applications for computational
chemistry, finite element analysis, and fluid dynamics, many solutions are
now available for the MCAD/CAE, pharmaceutical, biotech, and electronic
design industries. The cost of annual supercomputer maintenance alone can
justify the price of an AlphaServer 8400. (See the "AlphaServer 8400
Delivers Mainframe Performance for Less Cost" article in this issue.)

Users have never had a better opportunity to lower their operating and
maintenance costs and at the same time be provided with higher performing
and more reliable systems. The AlphaServer 8400 offers up to four times the
commercial performance of the VAX 7000 Model 610 and up to six times the
performance in technical workloads. It also offers up to five times the I/O
as the DEC 7000 systems. If IT managers are being asked to service more
demanding applications, more users, and larger storage on a decreased
budget, this enterprise server can complement any OpenVMS environment while
preserving investments in hardware, applications, data, networks, clusters,
and peripherals. The AlphaServer 8400 supports XMI, Futurebus+, and now PCI
I/O. (See the "Upgrading to AlphaServer 8200 and 8400 Systems" article in
this issue.)

