AlphaServer 8200 5/300 Server

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Over 2000 transactions per second, 3.6 GF (gigaflops), and 1.2 GB of I/O
   per second -- two to four times faster than competitive products

o  With up to six processors or 6 GB of memory, this high-end
   system offers small enterprises and large departments the most powerful,
   expandable, and reliable office environment server at the best
   price/performance

o  Users can now distribute demanding business critical applications, such
   as decision support, large database, and complex simulation
   applications -- down to the office

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new AlphaServer 8200 5/300 server offers up to six of the world's
fastest microprocessors, the Alpha 21164. With the enormous capacity of the
Alpha 64-bit architecture, up to 6 GB of memory, and PCI I/O of up to 108
slots, this server offers the largest and most complex applications the room
to grow.

Running the OpenVMS or Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) operating systems,
this server offers the reliability and availability features users require
for bet-your-business environments. These include clusters, hot swap disks,
RAID, redundant power, ECC memory and data paths, fault management, and
uninterruptible power systems -- all in a cabinet server that has been
priced to be the price/performance leader for systems in this price range.

Each AlphaServer 8200 base system includes a five-slot system bus, a 2 GB
SCSI system disk, an in-cabinet CD-ROM reader, an integrated I/O module with
three FWD SCSI ports, one single-ended SCSI port, two Ethernet ports, one
I/O hose port on-board (for connection to a 12-slot PCI), and optional
connectivity for FDDI and Prestoserve daughter cards. Additionally, the 8200
includes a choice of OpenVMS or Digital UNIX base operating system licenses,
a NAS 200 license, a one-year hardware warranty, and a 90-day software
warranty.

BENEFITS

Small enterprises and large departments now have a server with unprecedented
performance, capacity, and reliability for applications. Large database
support, complex simulations, data warehousing, and decision support are
just a few examples of the kinds of applications that the AlphaServer 8200
5/300 can run with ease. Also, with up to 6 GB of memory, this server can
provide all the benefits that Very Large Memory/Very Large Database
(VML/VLDB) systems provide.

For technical/scientific users, the AlphaServer 8200 provides supercomputer
class performance in the office. Its single processor floating point
performance eclipses that of competitive products in all the generic
benchmarks and will outperform them at the application level as well. With
up to six processors and up to 160 GB of storage in a single cabinet, the
new server delivers 3.6 GF of performance and the best price/performance
right to a user's fingertips.

