AlphaServer 8400 and 8200 High Performance Power

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Best price/performance

o  Sixty-one percent faster floating point performance than SGI
   PowerChallenge XL

o  One hundred percent faster LINPACK 1000 x 1000 than CRAY J90

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Users of high performance systems are interested primarily in
price/performance. The AlphaServer 8400 and 8200 are second to none in both
categories. Coupled with a strong portfolio of compute intensive
applications optimized for Alpha systems (see list at end of article), users
have an unprecedented advantage over the competition.

The AlphaServer 8400 and 8200 also offer outstanding investment protection
and growth potential. For smaller workloads or less complex simulations,
users can begin with the AlphaServer 8200 system. This system is designed
with less expandability (5 slots for  CPU, memory, and I/O boards), but
still can house up to 6 CPUs (3.6 GF of peak performance), 6 GB of memory or
additional I/O boards. For organizations with many users, larger workloads,
and more complex simulations, the AlphaServer 8400 system is the best
choice. With 9 slots, this system can handle up to 12 CPUs (7.2 GF), 14 GB
of memory, or more I/O slots.

There are also PCI based memory channel options for clustering (PID) that
are coming soon. PCI memory channel will allow clusters of AlphaServer
systems to be built, promising power up to 56 GF. Today's AlphaServer
systems combined with memory channel provide users with a flexible growth
path to unprecendented levels of power.

BENEFITS

AlphaServer 8400 and 8200 systems provide users with powerful yet affordable
systems. The increased memory capacity, CPU number and performance, and
faster I/O bandwidth means much faster turnaround time for important
applications.

The AlphaServer systems can also increase the efficiency of existing systems
by offloading smaller jobs that underutilize the expensive machines.

