AlphaServer 2100 Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  AlphaServer 2100 5/250 manages up to 1,200 transactions per second, with
   up to 4 symmetric multiprocessing Alpha 21164 processors

o  AlphaServer 2100 4/233 manages up to 675 transactions per second, with up
   to 4 symmetric multiprocessing processors

o  All entry configurations of AlphaServer 2100 systems are fast wide SCSI-2
   storage capable

o  New high performance PCI fast wide SCSI-2 options

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is enhancing its award-winning AlphaServer 2100 family with the
addition of higher performance models that support up to four processors
with symmetric multiprocessing. These new models continue the tradition of
delivering leadership performance and price/performance, as well as
providing cost effective processor upgrades. They are binary compatible with
the other members of the AlphaServer family, and are covered by Digital's
superior three-year, onsite, next-business-day-response-time hardware
warranty. These systems all use the same industry-standard PCI and EISA I/O,
deliver the same advanced reliability and availability features, and support
Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1), OpenVMS, and Windows NT Server
software environments.

The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 has the same characteristics as the other
AlphaServer 2100 systems, but provides significantly increased performance
through its use of the new Alpha 21164 microprocessor, at 250 MHz with a 4
MB third level (off chip) cache. The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 is binary
compatible with the other members of the AlphaServer family. The AlphaServer
2100 4/200, 4/233, and 4/275 may be upgraded to the faster processor through
a simple, cost effective processor board swap.

The AlphaServer 2100 4/233 is the new entry system for the AlphaServer 2100
family, replacing the AlphaServer 2100 4/200 model. It uses the Alpha 21064A
microprocessor at 233 MHz with a 1 MB secondary cache, and is binary
compatible with the other members of the AlphaServer family. This system
provides a performance boost over its predecessor at the same price.

To complement high performance PCI fast wide SCSI-2 storage options, the
entry configurations of all the AlphaServer 2100 systems now include a fast
wide SCSI-2 capable storage enclosure and a 2 GB wide capable SCSI disk.
Although the entry configurations are fast wide capable, the disk runs in
fast narrow mode when connected to the built-in fast narrow SCSI-2
controller.

Additional high performance PCI storage options are being added to Digital's
offerings. The new PCI fast wide single-ended SCSI-2 adapters (KZPSC)
support RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, and 5. The single channel KZPSC supports up
to 7 disks and the three-channel model supports up to 21 disks.

Another PCI option, the KZPSA, supports fast wide differential SCSI-2
storage with up to seven devices. This option is the same adapter that is
used for DECsafe Available Server software. For more information, see the
"DECsafe Available Server V1.2 for DEC OSF/1" article in the March 1995
issue of Sales Update.

BENEFITS

In the current highly competitive, rapidly changing business climate,
critical applications demand more from the systems that support them. Users
demand quick response times, fast application processing, and uninterrupted
service. IT and system managers demand a computing environment that
satisfies users and can incrementally, cost effectively expand as the
business grows -- while preserving current investments.

AlphaServer 2100 systems are optimized to support these computing
environments. With their Alpha central processors, symmetric multiprocessing
with up to four processors, and high performance, industry-standard PCI I/O,
the AlphaServer 2100 systems provide exceptional throughput to meet rigorous
application processing requirements and cost effective incremental expansion
of system capacity as computing requirements increase. With these features
and in-cabinet processor upgrades to ever faster Alpha processors, the
AlphaServer 2100 systems provide a very high degree of investment
protection.

Users expect systems and their data to be available all the time. The
AlphaServer 2100 systems address this requirement with a range of high
reliability functions built into the systems, and a cost effective storage
subsystem incorporating up to 16 hot swap disks and controller-based RAID to
provide very high data integrity. The next step is high availability
computing environments consisting of multiple systems, which Digital
provides through its industry leadership clusters technology.

With this scope of capabilities, AlphaServer 2100 systems deliver high
productivity for business operations, cost effective solutions for computing
challenges, and safeguards for valuable business information.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The AlphaServer 2100 4/233 and 4/275 systems are available now through
Digital, its authorized business partners, and through the DECdirect
service. The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 system will begin shipping in May 1995
with Digital UNIX and OpenVMS operating systems, and will be available with
Windows NT Server sometime between July and September 1995. Add-in
processors for all AlphaServer 2100 systems are available now. Processor
upgrades from the AlphaServer 2100 4/200, 4/233, and the 4/275 to the 5/250
will be available sometime between July and September 1995. AlphaServer 2100
5/250 ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE systems will be available sometime between July and
September 1995.

