Storage

The phase-in of support for fast wide SCSI-2 storage and larger capacity
disks on the AlphaServer 2100 systems is beginning. Fast wide SCSI-2 storage
is supported by a combination of the KZPSC fast wide/narrow RAID PCI
controllers and the RZ28-VW 2.1 GB fast wide SCSI-2 disk. This storage is
supported inside the new AlphaServer 2100 wide capable system pedestals as
well as in the BA356 wide storage expansion pedestal. This combination is
supported by Digital UNIX and Windows NT systems now, and will be supported
by OpenVMS systems in May 1995.

Fast wide differential SCSI-2 storage is supported by a combination of the
KZPSA fast wide differential PCI controller, the DWZZB wide differential to
wide single-ended converter, the BA356 wide storage pedestal, and the
RZ28-VW 2.1 GB fast wide SCSI-2 disk. This storage is supported external to
the system pedestal. This combination is supported by Digital UNIX and
Windows NT systems now, and will be supported by OpenVMS systems in May
1995.

For large storage, high performance, and the best price per megabyte, the
RZ29B 4.3 GB fast SCSI-2 disk is the best choice. This new disk is supported
on the AlphaServer 2100 systems when connected to the integral fast SCSI-2
controller or the KZPAA fast SCSI-2 PCI controller. The RZ29B connected to
