AlphaServer 2100 Rackmount and Cabinet Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Same functionality as similarly configured pedestal system

o  Large storage capability, up to 172 GB in a single 67-inch cabinet

o  Ideal for high availability configurations, 3 node, 12 CPU cluster in a
   single cabinet

o  Conforms to ANSI/EIA standard for 19-inch rackmount

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 has the same characteristics as the other
AlphaServer 2100 systems, but provides significantly increased performance
through its use of the new Alpha 21164 at 250 MHz with a 4 MB third level
(off chip) cache. It is binary compatible with the other members of the
AlphaServer family.

The AlphaServer 2100 4/233 is the new entry system for the AlphaServer 2100
family, replacing the AlphaServer 2100 4/200 model. It uses the Alpha 21064A
processor with a 1 MB secondary cache and is binary compatible with the
other members of the AlphaServer systems family.

The AlphaServer 2100 Cabinet system also has expanded storage capability,
allowing a single AlphaServer 2100 Rackmount system to be configured in a
67-inch high cabinet, with up to 172 GB of fixed disk storage using 2 GB
StorageWorks drives.

The new PCI fast wide single-ended SCSI-2 adapters (KZPSC) support RAID
levels 0, 1, 0+1, and 5. The single channel KZPSC supports up to 7 disks and
the three-channel model supports up to 21 disks. These options will be
delivered on a custom quote basis at this time because of cable length
constraints with the AlphaServer 2100 Cabinet systems.

BENEFITS

The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 Rackmount and the associated AlphaServer 2100
5/250 Cabinet packaged systems allow users to create high availability
configurations more easily, such as clusters for OpenVMS or DECsafe
software, as well as other configurations that require large amounts of
storage. The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 Cabinet consists of at least one
AlphaServer 2100 5/250 Rackmount as well as rackmount storage and other
associated equipment mounted in a standard Digital cabinet.

Designed with high availability in mind, the AlphaServer 2100 Cabinet system
provides a range of high reliability and availability functions built into
the systems such as:

o  Cost effective storage subsystems that incorporate hot swap disks and
   controller-based RAID to provide very high data integrity.

o  The AlphaServer 2100 Rackmount system was designed with minimal internal
   storage. This feature allows for the creation of high availability
   configurations independent of the storage.

o  The AlphaServer 2100 Rackmount system supports optional fully redundant
   power supplies in a N+1 arrangement, allowing a single power supply to
   support a fully loaded system. The AlphaServer 2100 Cabinet system also
   allows redundant power supplies for StorageWorks shelves.

o  Optional rackmounted UPS systems.

o  Dual host AlphaServer 2100 Cabinet system requires the space of a
   comparable pedestal configuration, while providing more storage
   capability.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The AlphaServer 2100 4/233 Rackmount and Cabinet systems are available now.
The AlphaServer 2100 5/250 system will begin shipping in May 1995 with
Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) and OpenVMS Alpha platforms.

