AlphaServer 2000 Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  AlphaServer 2000 4/275 manages up to 625 transactions per second with up
   to 2 symmetric multiprocessing processors

o  AlphaServer 2000 4/233 manages up to 400 transactions per second with up
   to 2 symmetric multiprocessing processors

o  Up to 1 GB of memory now supported in all AlphaServer 2000 models

o  All entry configurations are fast wide SCSI-2 storage capable

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is enhancing its AlphaServer 2000 family with the addition of higher
performance models all supporting up to two processors with symmetric
multiprocessing. These new models continue the tradition of delivering
leadership performance and price/performance, providing cost effective
processor upgrades, and are binary compatible with the other members of the
AlphaServer family. They also are covered by Digital's superior three-year
onsite, next-business-day-response-time hardware warranty.

These systems all use the same industry-standard PCI and EISA I/O, deliver
the same advanced reliability and availability features, and support Digital
UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1), OpenVMS, and Windows NT Server software
environments.

The new higher performance AlphaServer 2000 4/275 is the Alpha 21064A
microprocessor at 275 MHz with a 4 MB secondary cache in the familiar
AlphaServer 2000 package. This system uses the same 4/275 add-in processor
as the AlphaServer 2100 4/275. The AlphaServer 2000 4/200 may be upgraded to
the faster processor through a simple, cost effective processor board swap.

The AlphaServer 2000 4/233 is the new entry system for the AlphaServer 2000
family, replacing the AlphaServer 2000 4/200 model. It uses the Alpha 21064A
microprocessor at 233 MHz with a 1 MB secondary cache and is binary
compatible with the other members of the AlphaServer systems family. This
system provides more performance than its predecessor at the same price.

Maximum memory of 1 GB is achieved by building up from the entry systems
containing 128 MB of memory.

To complement high performance PCI fast wide SCSI-2 storage options, the
entry configurations of all the AlphaServer 2000 systems now include a fast
wide SCSI-2 capable storage enclosure and a 2 GB wide capable SCSI disk.
Although the entry configurations are fast wide capable, the disk runs in
fast narrow mode when connected to the built-in fast narrow SCSI-2
controller.

Additional high performance PCI storage options are being added to Digital's
offerings. The new PCI fast wide single-ended SCSI-2 adapters (KZPSC)
support RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, and 5. The single channel KZPSC supports up
to 7 disks and the three-channel model supports up to 21 disks.

Another PCI option, the KZPSA, supports fast wide differential SCSI-2
storage with up to seven devices. This option is the same adapter that is
used for DECsafe Available Server software. For more information, please see
the "DECsafe Available Server V1.2 for DEC OSF/1" article in the March 1995
Sales Update.

BENEFITS

In the current competitive and rapidly changing business climate, critical
applications demand more from the systems that support them. Users demand
quick response times, fast application processing, and uninterrupted
service. IT and system managers demand a computing environment that
satisfies users and can incrementally and cost effectively expand as the
business grows -- while preserving current investments. This environment
needs to be purchased and supported for the least amount of money.

AlphaServer 2000 systems are optimized to support these computing
environments. With their Alpha central processors, an optional second
processor with symmetric multiprocessing, and high performance,
industry-standard PCI I/O, the AlphaServer 2000 systems provide high
throughput to meet rigorous application processing requirements and cost
effective incremental expansion of system capacity as computing requirements
increase. With these features and in-cabinet processor upgrades to ever
faster Alpha processors, the AlphaServer 2000 systems provide a very high
degree of investment protection.

Users expect systems and their data to be available all the time. The
AlphaServer 2000 systems address this requirement with a range of high
reliability functions built into the systems, and a cost effective storage
subsystem incorporating up to eight hot swap disks and controller-based RAID
to provide very high data integrity. The next step is high availability
computing environments, consisting of multiple systems which Digital
provides through its industry leadership cluster technology.

With these capabilities, AlphaServer 2000 systems deliver high productivity
for business operations, cost effective solutions for computing challenges,
and safeguards for valuable business information.

