AlphaStation 250 4/266 Midrange Performance Workstation

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Fastest desktop workstation for the demanding engineer and scientist

o  Midrange PCI based Alpha client system supporting Digital UNIX, OpenVMS,
   and Windows NT Workstation environments

o  Industry leading price/performance will support 3D solids modeling (new
   graphics board to be available in July)

o  Three-year hardware warranty and 90-day telephone advisory software
   support included

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaStation 250 4/266 workstation, the newest member of the
AlphaStation family, is housed in a low-profile desktop enclosure that
accepts both PCI and ISA options available from Digital and its business
partners. The new workstation is ideal for users who demand high performance
and graphics, and require all the benefits of industry standard option
support. The system supports Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1), OpenVMS, and
Microsoft Windows NT operating systems.

Designed for overall balanced performance, the AlphaStation 250 4/266
includes 2 MB of on-board cache, a 128-bit wide memory bus, support for 256
MB of memory with future support for up to 512 MB, and the PCI industry
standard high performance I/O bus. The system delivers leadership CPU
performance at 198 SPECint92 and 262 SPECfp92.

The AlphaStation 250 4/266 is multimedia ready and supports the newest
collaboration software and video options. Users can easily add video capture
for video conferencing or multimedia authoring with the new FullVideo
Supreme video input/output PCI option for Digital UNIX based systems (see
article on FullVideo Supreme in this issue).

BENEFITS

o  Performance -- supports the most intensive applications in technical
   environments, including MCAD, ECAD, geographic information systems, and
   science and research.

o  Investment protection -- binary compatible with the Alpha family; three
   I/O slots for a variety of PCI/ISA options; and the industry's best
   warranty.

o  Price -- delivers superior performance and price/performance at an
   entry-level price.

o  Open system -- offers industry standard PCI/ISA options and choice of
   operating systems, available through a variety of suppliers.

