mach64 Graphics Accelerator for AlphaStation 200 4/100

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Industry's fastest DRAM graphics accelerators now on AlphaStation 200
   4/100

o  Immediately available for use under Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT
   systems

o  Enables a cost effective transition from x86 to RISC platforms

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The mach64 graphics accelerator is a cost effective, single-slot PCI-bus
graphical user interface (GUI) accelerator for use in mainstream 2D
applications. With 2 MB of DRAM, the mach64 option is capable of operation
in both 8-plane and 24-plane operation, with flicker-free refresh rates up
to 80 Hz.

The DRAM-based mach64 has proven itself very successful in the PC arena,
having earned both "Editor's Choice" in PC Magazine (12/94) and "Byte Best"
in Byte magazine (2/95). Making a transition into the entry-workstation
space with an Xmark93 of 3.7, the mach64 continues to prove itself
well-suited for use in entry-CAD, process control, general business, and
desktop publishing applications.

BENEFITS

o  Best DRAM graphics performance value presently on the market

o  Outstanding price/performance for entry-level clients

o  Cost effective transition from x86 to RISC platforms

PRODUCT POSITIONING

The following performance comparisons are based on AlphaStation 200 4/100
platform.

Product	    Domain            Key Performance Metrics

mach64	    2D, DRAM, PCI     Xmark93:	  3.7
DEC864	    2D, DRAM, PCI     Xmark93:	  N/A, Windows NT only
ZLXp-E1	    2D/3D, VRAM, PCI  Xmark93:	  9.1

In general, relative positioning of the PCI graphics options for the
AlphaStation platform is as follows:

o  For Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) and OpenVMS systems
   requiring highly competitive, cost effective graphics for use in general
   2D, entry-CAD, or business applications, the option of choice is the
   mach64 (PB2GA-FA/FV).

o  For Windows NT systems requiring highly competitive, cost effective
   graphics for use in general 2D, entry-CAD, or business applications, the
   option of choice is the DEC864 (PBXGA-JA). The DEC864 is supported under
   Windows NT only.

o  For Digital UNIX and OpenVMS systems requiring exceptional 2D vector or
   Xmark93 performance for use in high performance 2D, entry-CAD, or
   visualization applications, the option of choice is the ZLXp-E1
   (PBXGA-AA).

o  For Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT systems requiring either double
   buffering or high spatial resolution and 24 bit true color for use in
   high performance 2D, entry-3D CAD, or visualization applications, the
   option of choice is the ZLXp-E2 (PBXGA-BA).

o  For Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT systems requiring 24 bit
   Z-buffering for fast 3D vector/triangle performance for use in entry-3D
   CAD or OpenGL applications, the option of choice is the ZLXp-E3
   (PBXGA-CA).

o  For Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT systems requiring multihead
   configurations, the only option that supports multiple screens is the
   ZLXp-Ex (PBXGA-Ax).

Applications written to run on the ZLXp-E1 under X11 will run on the mach64
option, albeit at lower X-performance. For applications that leverage any
X-extensions, OpenGL, PEX, or double/Z-buffering, the mach64 option is not
recommended.

