PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The VAX 4000 Model 106A combines the power of a 10 ns (nanosecond) NVAX
CMOS-4 processor, the richness of DSSI and DSSI VMSclustering, the maturity
of OpenVMS software, and the ease of Q-bus connectivity with low-cost
memory, power, and packaging. The Model 106A features two major improvements
over the Model 105A: its CPU is 20 percent faster (10 ns) than the Model
105A (12 ns); and it has an enhanced DSSI I/O cable box that allows more
flexible DSSI clustering capabilites.

In addition, Digital is offering the VAX 4000 Models 106A, 505A, and 705A
with a new three-year hardware warranty as the standard warranty that comes
with the systems, with no increase in price. This enhancement will decrease
the cost of ownership of these powerful systems that drive users'
increasingly complex databases and growing PC LANs. Installation is no
longer included in the Standard Price but can be purchased separately.

The Model 705A, the highest performing member of the VAX 4000 family, runs
at 280 transactions per second and 45 VUPS. Like all VAX 4000 pedestal
systems, it includes two on-board high speed DSSI controllers, with an
option for two additional DSSI controllers. In addition to being configured
with RF36E disk drives, each controller can now be connected to the recently
announced HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI controllers. Thus, all of Digital's industry
standard SCSI devices are available for VAX 4000 systems.

The VAX 4000 Model 505A achieves an impressive 200 transactions per second
and provides a cost effective platform like the Model 705A, with Q-bus
expansion and DSSI clustering.

