now with shipping to begin May 19. They will be available through Digital
and its business partners. Digital will continue to offer VAX 4000 ADVANTAGE
SERVER Packages, which have been re-packaged; but is eliminating VAX 4000
Base System Packages to reduce the number of variants and simplify ordering.

The VAX 4000 family continues to offer multiple upgrade paths to preserve
users' investments in systems, storage, and other options (see the "VAX to
VAX Upgrades" article in this issue for additional information).

Digital is also continuing to meet user requirements for SCSI disks, tapes,
and CD-ROMs on all VAX 4000 systems. With the HSD05 DSSI-to-SCSI
controllers, Model 505A and 705A users can now employ Digital industry
standard SCSI devices internally (in the system enclosure; see the HSD05
articles in the March 21, 1994 and May 16, 1994 issues of Sales Update) or
externally. Model 106A users will be able to employ the HSD05 controller
