StorageWorks TL810 Automated Tape Library

HIGHLIGHTS

o  New member of the Digital Linear Tape automated tape library family

o  Low cost, high capacity, reliable automated mass storage for departmental
   data management applications

o  Integrates automated backup, archiving, and hierarchical storage
   management to department operations while keeping pace with larger-scale
   enterprise-wide mass storage schemes

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The second member of Digital's library family, the TL810 library, has a
smaller capacity, higher ratio of drive-to-cartridge units and a smaller
footprint than the high-capacity TL820 library. With a capacity of 52
cartridges and 4 Digital Linear Tape (DLT) TZ87 drives, the TL810 library
offers a range of capacity from 0.5 to 1.0 TB (terabytes). This fully
automated storage library includes the robotic hardware and firmware
necessary to store and move up to 52 DLT cartridges, 4 of which are
contained in a built-in four-cartridge Load Port (Import/Export).

The TL810 adds a less expensive, faster access automated tape library to the
product family and is ideal for datacenter applications for Digital systems,
platforms, clusters, and networks. The unsurpassed speed, capacity, and
reliability of the DLT technology (ANSI standard), integrated with the
highly reliable proven robotics design, provide a high capacity, high
performance, quality product for departmental storage needs.

BENEFITS

Combined with Digital's POLYCENTER Storage Management software application
solutions, DECLS or third party applications, the TL810 tape library can
make backup, archive, and POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management
operations easy, quick, reliable, and cost effective.

o  Extends the benefits of automated storage management to department and
   client/server applications that are presently enjoyed by larger
   enterprisewide datacenters

o  Integrates automated backup and archiving to department operations

o  Protects against data loss by providing accurate, secure, auditable
   archiving and backup of information

o  Provides near-online storage in huge capacities but with a small
   footprint for datacenter, network, and server applications

o  Boosts productivity and lowers costs for datacenter management and
   operations through automated access to data

o  Provides cost effective and reliable storage for POLYCENTER Hierarchical
   Storage Manager applications

o  Provides (with appropriate applications support) built-in Automatic Drive
   Cleaning feature that allows high availability of drives without operator
   intervention

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TL810 will be available for order on April 11, 1995 with a 90-day
leadtime with expected deliveries beginning in July 1995. The TL810 will
ship with four TZ87 drives installed in the system as well as one cleaning
cartridge and one DLT data cartridge. Application software and external
cabling or adapters and controllers must be ordered separately.

