DWZZB 16-bit SCSI Bus Extender and Signal Converter

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Handles the more powerful 16-bit SCSI buses as well as 8-bit buses

o  Handles data rates up to 20 MB per second on Fast SCSI, and is fully
   compatible with the 2- to 5-MB per second data rates of earlier SCSI
   interconnects

o  Extends SCSI buses from 3 or 6 meters to 25 meters

o  Accepts conventional single-ended signals on one end and differential
   signals on the other end

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DWZZB is a differential to single-ended SCSI bus extender and signal
converter. It is an 8 or 16 bits Fast Wide Differential SCSI on one side and
an 8 or 16 bits single-ended SCSI on the other side. The DWZZB is SCSI-3
(ANSI X3T9.2-10R3) compliant, can handle data rates up to 20 (16-bit) MB per
second, and operates transparently to the SCSI bus. The product fully
supports all of the latest SCSI-3 bus phases as well as all earlier standard
SCSI compatible implementations, back to SASI.

Applications of the DWZZB include:

o  Connecting a user supplied 16-bit differential device to a 16-bit
   single-ended adapter.
o  Extending a 16-bit SCSI single-ended bus so that very loud devices may be
   located in a lights-out closet or away from noise-sensitive work spaces.
o  Creating "clumps" with UNIX systems so that non-dynamic disk sharing can
   occur should one of two worksystems fail.
o  Centrally locating devices for several members of a workgroup for
   administrative or security control.

The DWZZB family consists of the DWZZB-AA standalone product, the DWZZB-MA
module for OEM use, and the DWZZB-VW for StorageWorks pedestals and shelves.

DWZZB-AA Standalone Product

With a built-in universal power supply, the DWZZB-AA is self-contained. It
meets general purpose SCSI bus length and signal conversion needs, and can
be used with any device that is SCSI-2 compatible.

DWZZB-MA Module for OEM Use

The DWZZB-MA is the first OEM SCSI signal converter that operates at 20 MB
per second and is fully ANSI compliant. Designed and manufactured by
Digital, the DWZZB-MA consists of the basic module for embedded applications
and requires that the OEM or System Integrator supply power and packaging.

DWZZB-VW for StorageWorks Pedestals and Shelves

The DWZZB-VW occupies a single Storage Building Block (SBB) slot in the new
BA356 StorageWorks Deskside Wide Expansion Pedestal, and also works in BA350
shelves. It converts the single-ended disks and tapes in the shelf to the
differential SCSI signal standards, so that the need to connect the BA356 to
a differential host adapter as much as 25 meters (88 feet) away can be
accommodated.

BENEFITS

The DWZZB can be used to connect the widening range of available
differential SCSI storage devices and subsystems to single-ended hosts. It
can also be used to free a system of the SCSI bus length limit, and to
locate SCSI devices over 170 feet apart using synchronous transfers. Its
unique patent-pending features allow maximum extension of the SCSI bus with
no performance degradation. Also, no changes are required to existing
devices or software; the DWZZB does not occupy a SCSI bus node.

Other built-in features and their benefits include:

o  Glitch free power-up -- Drivers designed to not glitch the bus when
   the DWZZB is powered up.
o  Edge rate control -- Slower rise and fall time for the signal drivers
   contributes less ringing than fast edge drivers.
o  Active negation of signals -- Drive signals to the off condition, not
   just taking the driver out of saturation.
o  Active SCSI bus termination -- Precise termination impedance and
   fixed and limited load currents.
o  Bus signals wired only to a driver and a hysteresis receiver -- Less
   noise effect, less bus capacitance, less stub length, other internal etch
   wiring becomes less critical.
o  Board responds to SCSI RESET, BUS FREE, and POWER RESET -- Won't hang the
   bus.
o  Direct support of the 68 pin SCSI-3 Connector.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DWZZB is available now.

Order No.        Description

		 16-BIT SCSI BUS EXTENDER AND SIGNAL
                 CONVERTER:
