PORTswitch 900 Family of Per-port Switching Products

HIGHLIGHTS

o  High density, per-port configurable repeaters for the three standard
   cable media types, UTP, fiber optic, and coax

o  Per-port and configuration switching, allowing for the implementation of
   virtual LANs

o  Fiber optic and UTP versions support redundant, fault tolerant repeater
   to repeater links

o  Secure access control on each port

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The PORTswitch 900 family are DEChub 900 single slot hub products. They
support configuration switching, providing the flexibility to logically
interconnect any combination of externally accessible ports onto any of six
available physical internal LAN segments. These six internal Ethernet
segments can be switched to dedicated DEChub backplane Ethernet segments
through software. All PORTswitch 900 products have built-in industry
standard Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) management agents,
allowing for the gathering of management statistics on a per-port basis
using a variety of SNMP management applications.

As with all DEChub 900 products, these single slot hub products can be
installed in the multi-slot DEChub 900 MultiSwitch or in a single slot
DEChub ONE chassis for a standalone, stackable solution.

The PORTswitch family of per-port switching modules comprises three
different products, one of each supporting the three standard Ethernet cable
media types: UTP/10Base-T, fiber optic/10Base-FL/FOIRL, and ThinWire
coax/10Base-2.

Three Product Variants

o  PORTswitch 900TP is a port-switchable, 32-port, 10Base-T Ethernet
   repeater with shielded, 8 pin MJ, RJ45-type connectors.

o  PORTswitch 900CP is a port-switchable, 16-port, ThinWire coax, 10Base-2
   Ethernet repeater with BNC connectors.

o  PORTswitch 900FP is a new name for the currently available DECrepeater
   900FP and is a port-switchable, 12-port 10Base-FL repeater with ST style
   connectors.

BENEFITS

o  Simplify the administration of network changes -- Software invoked port
   switching simplifies and reduces the cost of adminstrating network adds,
   moves, and changes by eliminating the necessity of trips to wiring closet
   to physically reconfigure LAN connections.

o  Implement Virtual LANs today -- Work teams can be easily configured onto
   their own LAN, optimizing current network bandwidth and providing team
   members with a more responsive and secure network.

o  Optimize available network bandwidth to users -- Per-port switching
   allows unprecedented flexibility in configuring networks and allocating
   network bandwidth to users that need it. Software invoked LAN
   segmentation using HUBwatch allows a network administrator to reconfigure
   the number of users on a particular LAN segment or move users to another
   LAN segment. This results in more bandwidth available to a fewer number
   of users per segment, thus increasing network efficiency and network
   response time for those attached user groups.

o  Hub-based or standalone configurations -- This unique DEChub capability
   maximizes users' options to buy only what they need and protects their
   investment by eliminating additional cost or obsolescence when changing
   from one configuration to the other.

o  Secure access on a per-port basis -- Security at the port level provides
   a network manager with the capability to prevent both network broadcast
   intrusion and eavesdropping. Broadcast intrusion protection detects
   unauthorized devices connected to a port. Eavesdropping protection
   prevents the transmission of data to unauthorized devices attempting to
   access the data stream. This feature is fully controllable via HUBwatch
   software.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The PORTswitch 900 family of per-port switching products will be available
in June 1995 primarily through Digital's authorized resellers, value-added
resellers, OEMs, and wholesale distributors.

