HUBwatch V4.0 Enables Virtual LANs on a PC

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Now supports PORTswitch 900TP and CP, GIGAswitch/ATM, DECconcentrator
   900TH, DECmau 900TH, and DECserver 900GM

o  Adds functions of Virtual LANs, FDDI trees, DECrepeater 90TS/FS manage
   DECrepeater 90s, intelligent agents, repeater loop prevention, secure
   address learning, FDDI ring patching, and Token Ring management

o  New PC based workgroup managers Novell NMS and ManageWORKS

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

HUBwatch V4.0 is element network management software that provides a
powerful, low cost, graphical, Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP)
interface to control Digital's network hardware. It lets users create and
manage Virtual LANs in a DEChub 900 MultiSwitch by interconnecting ports,
modules, and LAN segments with a simple drag-and-drop operation. HUBwatch
V4.0 has the same functionality and interface on Windows, UNIX, and OpenVMS
platforms. It can be run standalone or launched by common workgroup or
enterprise managers. All this functionality, including management of
GIGAswitch/FDDI and GIGAswitch/ATM, can run on an existing PC.

BENEFITS

o  Virtual LANs -- Using PORTswitches (per port switching repeaters) and the
   DEChub 900 MultiSwitch, individual repeater ports can be placed on
   different LAN segments and interconnected with switches to balance
   traffic. HUBwatch V4.0 provides easy adds, moves, changes, bandwidth
   optimization, and security in a cost effective manner.

o  Increased options for bandwidth optimization -- HUBwatch V4.0 now
   supports the full range of Digital switches, from port level
   configuration switches, such as the PORTswitch 900TP and 900CP, to
   enterprise level LAN switches such as GIGAswitch/ATM. It also provides
   the lowest cost switch management software. (HUBwatch management of
   GIGAswitch/ATM is currently available only on Windows.)

o  Lower cost -- With the firmware upgrade included in HUBwatch V4.0,
   DECrepeater 90TS and 90FS can manage DECrepeater 90s. This is part of
   Digital's commitment to minimize the cost of management by distributing
   agents to each module. A DECagent 90 is no longer needed to manage
   DECrepeater 90s.

o  PC based workgroup management -- Novell's NMS and Digital's ManageWORKS
   can now launch HUBwatch software along with HP OpenView. Both NMS and
   ManageWORKS products can automatically generate a network map with icons
   for DEChub and GIGAswitch products and can "browse" SNMP MIBs. When a
   Digital icon is selected, HUBwatch software is launched to manage the
   device. NMS and ManageWORKS products also support LAN administration as
   well as device management.

o  Intelligent agents -- With the firmware upgrade included in HUBwatch
   V4.0, intelligent agents in the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch and each repeater
   can provide module and port level alarms for fault isolation and traffic
   monitoring. PROBEwatch can be launched from HUBwatch for Windows and
   HUBwatch for Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) software by
   clicking on the DECPACKETPROBE software. Both these features reduce
   management traffic while providing exception reporting. (DECrepeater
   90C/T/FL/FA does not have intelligent agents.)

o  Increased utility of existing hardware -- The HUBloader software,
   included in HUBwatch V4.0, allows easy point and click firmware upgrades.
   The firmware in the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch manager has been upgraded to
   prevent the creation of repeater loops. The firmware in repeaters has
   been upgraded to enable automatic learning of secure port addresses.

o  Increased FDDI functionality -- HUBwatch V4.0 manages the DECconcentrator
   900TH, a 14 port UTP FDDI concentrator. In addition, the firmware has
   been upgraded to support FDDI trees as well as dual rings for the
   DECconcentrator 900TH and DECconcentrator 900MX, and FDDI auto-recovery.
   (A fault is automatically patched around by this feature.)

o  Token Ring management -- The newly announced DECmau 900TH (24 ports with
   active RI/RO) has an integral SNMP agent that allows previously shipping
   Token Ring products (DECmau 900TL and DECrepeater 900TL/SL/FL) to be
   managed when installed in a DEChub 900 MultiSwitch. Two Token Ring
   segments are created in the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch backplane, plus
   automatic ring beaconing detection and ring mapping are enabled.

o  Access servers -- V4.0 adds management of the DECserver 900GM, a 32/16
   port server with modem control. Also, Telnet access is provided to all
   servers that support it (except DECserver 90L/L+).

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

HUBwatch V4.0 for Windows (SPD 37.87), Digital UNIX (SPD 46.65), and OpenVMS
VAX (SPD 45.74) platforms will be available in June 1995.

