Reliable Transaction Router V3.1 for Digital UNIX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Production release of Reliable Transaction Router middleware for Digital
   UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) based systems

o  Addition of management utilities for distributed environments

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Reliable Transaction Router software is middleware for distributed
client/server applications that require continuous availability, transaction
integrity, and scalable performance. It is intended for application
environments where downtime, lost data, or slow response time will affect
profits or customer satisfaction.

Reliable Transaction Router software provides reliable transactional
messaging between distributed client, router, and server systems.
Application software is insulated from the underlying complexity of the
network configuration. Reliable Transaction Router software detects failures
in the distributed environment and provides transparent failover and
transaction integrity. The product provides for flexible growth to high
performance or widely distributed environments, as business requirements
dictate.

Reliable Transaction Router middleware has been available on OpenVMS
software since 1991. V3.1 supports deployment of production applications on
Digital UNIX software. In addition, management utilities supporting
distributed environments have been added.

BENEFITS

Applications in the trading and exchanges, banking, transportation,
telecommunications, information services, and retail industries often
require the ability to execute transactions reliably, in realtime, without
interruption, across distributed systems.

Using Reliable Transaction Router middleware, users can:

o  Avoid the costs of downtime or lost data in distributed environments.
o  Gain competitive advantage by providing superior service levels.
o  Reduce development costs by focusing on applications versus
   infrastructure.
o  Protect their investments by using scalable, flexible middleware.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Reliable Transaction Router V3.1 for Digital UNIX software is available now.
Two licenses are available. A "Front End License" supports client
functionality. A "Back End License" supports client, router, and server
functionality, and is required for router or server systems.

