Leafbridge V2.0 Remote Bridge for Europe Only

HIGHLIGHTS

o					      Provides enhanced performance

o	Includes data compression, remote management, and dial-up and other
functionality -- with no modification in pricing

o     Totally compatible with V1.1; upgrade kit available for existing V1.1
users

o	      Interoperable with DECbrouter 90 and Cisco bridges and routers

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Small remote user sites typically do not have any networking expertise.
Leafbridge is a remote bridge that enables users to simply and cost
effectively interconnect a remote site -- consisting of PCs, workstations,
and video terminals -- with a central site via low speed lines.

Leafbridge provides a real "plug-and-forget" Ethernet-to-Ethernet connection
through a 9600 bits per second to 64 Kb (kilobits) per second synchronous
link. The product is easy to install, use, and manage.

New Features

o  Performance enhancement; filtering rate extended from 1,700 to 8,000
   frames per second
o  Data compression types supported:
   - Tinygram Compression
   - Protocol Field Compression
   - Address and Control Field Compression
   - Repetitive Pattern Suppression
   - Van-Jacobson like IP Compression
   - LAT Compression
o  Address filtering
o  Number of filters extended from 10 to 26
o  New user-friendly way to set up filters via 16 pre-configured filters
o  Remote management via Telnet
o  Support for SNMP MIB II and MIB Bridge standards
o  Anti-congestion mechanism
o  Dial-up capability
o  Support of ICMP standard (Ping command)
o  Local management command enhancement
o  Interoperability with DECbrouter 90 and Cisco bridges and routers

BENEFITS

Taking advantage of the performance enhancement and addition of bandwidth
optimization features -- such as data compression, address filtering, and an
anti-congestion mechanism -- users can now connect remote sites more
efficiently and cost effectively by using lower speed lines. Typically,
there is no networking expertise available at remote sites. With V2.0,
remote management via Telnet commands enables users to manage the remote
Leafbridge from the central site.

All of these new features are provided with no increase in price. In
addition, existing V1.1 users can migrate to V2.0 at a minimal cost. They
can choose either to use the trade-in program or upgrade the product
themselves.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Leafbridge V2.0 will be available now in Europe only. The product can be
plugged into a DEChub 90 backplane (which provides a power supply and
Ethernet link) or can be used as a standalone unit.

