CICS for Digital UNIX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  IBM's Customer Information Control System (CICS) has been ported to
   Digital UNIX based Alpha platform

o  Provides full CICS package, including CICS API for portability of
   applications, and InterSystem Communication for interoperability with
   mainframe CICS systems

o  Complements Digital's range of TP monitors available on Digital UNIX
   software

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

CICS for Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) software is Digital's port of
IBM's CICS application, the primary mainframe TP monitor software for the
past 25 years. The CICS solution involves user-written applications that
manage transactions entered at terminals or PCs. It provides the services
needed by those applications to retrieve and update data in files, and to
respond to the device that invoked the application. The software was
originally designed to support very large, centralized transaction
processing where the primary objectives are efficiency (speed) and data
integrity. It has been extended into the open systems arena with a portable,
standards based, client/server oriented version.

The CICS for Open Systems family, which includes CICS for Digital UNIX, has
been designed to take advantage of the industry standards for data
communications and distributed computing. It maintains existing APIs and
communications protocols to ensure applications portability from, and
interoperability with, existing CICS applications on mainframes and other
platforms.

Product Features

CICS for Digital UNIX software is based on IBM's AIX CICS/6000 product and
provides all the key features of the IBM CICS family. Compatibility with the
other CICS family products is provided through support for the CICS API, and
interoperability is supported through use of the CICS InterSystem
Communication (ISC) capability.

CICS features include:

o  CICS family API for portability of applications to and from CICS software
   on other platforms, including the full range of IBM mainframes and
   minicomputers, and systems from other vendors. The CICS API is supported
   for both COBOL and C programming languages. The use of COBOL requires the
   MicroFocus COBOL compiler and runtime support.

o  Support for a full range of popular relational databases accessed through
   CICS commands and SQL calls. Coordinated commitment and recovery of
   transactions is supported by the use of the X/OPEN XA interface. ORACLE
   and INFORMIX databases will be supported at first release, and additional
   databases will be supported soon thereafter.

o  Support for VSAM files through the Encina Structured File Server (SFS),
   which is supplied as part of the CICS Cell Server package.

o  Full interoperability with CICS applications running on mainframes, and
   distributed CICS family members through the ISC services over TCP/IP or
   SNA. This supports the distribution of data and transactions using the
   ISC features:

   - Transaction routing
   - Function shipping
   - Distributed program link
   - Asynchronous transaction processing
   - Distributed transaction processing; any conversion of data (for
     example, from ASCII to EBCDIC) is performed automatically using
     customer generated templates

o  Applications written using Basic Mapping Support (BMS) or direct terminal
   calls may be connected to a variety of terminals using the CICS Client
   interfaces (daemons) for:

   - ASCII terminals (such as VTs) and terminal emulators (PCs, X Windows
   software)
   - 3270 emulators using Telnet 3270 protocol
   - 3270 terminals connected through mainframes

   Additional terminals and graphical user interfaces (such as Motif or
   Windows software) may be supported by adding client applications
   programmed using the External Programming Interface (EPI) provided in the
   CICS Client package.

o  User-written clients on Digital UNIX based AlphaServer or AlphaStation
   systems may be attached to CICS application servers by using the External
   Call Interface (ECI) provided in the CICS Client package to communicate
   between the client and server over a TCP/IP link. CICS also supports ECI
   access to CICS Server applications from user-written clients, CICS OS/2
   systems, and other CICS Clients over SNA or TCP/IP links. These clients
   may be written to meet the user's graphical or object-oriented
   requirements.

o  System Management is provided by a specific CICS management tool that
   offers a graphical interface for ease of use. The management tool
   provides management for the complete CICS environment, including the DCE
   and Encina infrastructure. In addition, tools to assist in the migration
   of applications and data from the mainframe are included with CICS
   software.

BENEFITS

o  Investment protection for CICS applications and skills: Developer skills
   are preserved; source code and screen definitions do not change; and
   applications look and run the same for the end user.

o  CICS brand name recognition and conformance: Training costs are reduced;
   and wide industry experience and familiarity exists.

o  Growth opportunity: Supplements and interoperates with mainframe CICS
   software; and allows users to expand while moving to a better
   price/performance solution.

o  Users who downsize by re-hosting existing CICS applications will find
   that they can: Achieve significant savings that are either moved to the
   bottom line or invested in critical re-engineering activities to enhance
   the company's competitive position; free up IBM mainframe resources to
   avoid a costly upgrade, entirely replace the mainframe; or make room for
   other critical business processing; and maintain application support
   while moving to a better price/performance solution.

o  Alpha technology offers a scalable product line from desktop to
   datacenter; the 2 GB file size restriction imposed by mainframe and 32
   bit implementations is lifted -- without requiring changes to application
   source code

o  Industry leading price/performance and throughput of Alpha systems

o  Alpha offers the ability to connect to both mainframes and other
   platforms with strong networking products

o  Open systems and software protects the user's investment with an
   extensive selection of hardware platforms and software applications,
   tools, etc.

o  Access to Alpha technology, including clustering and journaling of file
   systems

o  An extensive array of systems integration resources are available through
   top quality firms as well as an entire industry of CICS based tools and
   applications

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

CICS for Digital UNIX is available now from Digital and resellers.

CICS is supplied in three license packages: CICS Cell Server, CICS Server,
and CICS Client. The CICS Cell Server License enables the CICS Server and
Encina SFS. The CICS Server License enables CICS software and the supporting
Encina components. The CICS Client License is a flat tiered capacity
license; it enables unlimited user access from VTs, TN3270, 3270s, and
user-written applications using the EPI or ECI API.

