Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX V1.5

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Intel Indeo compression and decompression and MPEG-1 decompression in
   software

o  Enhanced out-of-the-box applications for audio/video capture and display
   and video output

o  Audio Compression Manager for IMA ADPCM audio compression and
   decompression

o  Support for the FullVideo Supreme PCI video input/output option

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Multimedia Services V1.5 for Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1)
software (SPD 48.92.05) brings audio and video capabilities to Digital's
workstations, and provides a full programming library for use by developers
of new applications. Multimedia Services V1.5 provides support for the
built-in audio and optional audio/video hardware on Alpha workstations.

The application programming interface is based on the same multimedia
interface provided in Windows NT and Windows V3.1 operating systems,
including Video for Windows.

The following new features of Multimedia Services V1.5 are part of the
runtime environment included with every Digital UNIX packaged workstation:

o  Intel Indeo R3.1 and R3.2 software decompression and Indeo R3.2
   compression, allowing users to play back and create one of the most
   popular PC video file formats in the industry. Indeo files created on a
   PC now can play on Digital UNIX workstations and vice versa.

o  MPEG-1 software decompression to playback MPEG-1 audio/video files. Users
   can play files stored on the internet and CD-ROM formats on their Alpha
   workstations.

o  JPEG software compression to create JPEG files without the need of a JPEG
   hardware option (complements JPEG software playback capabilities already
   provided).

o  AlphaVCR, an application with a variety of features:

   - Play live video and audio.
   - Record video in AVI formats, including YUV and JPEG.
   - Play back audio and video files containing JPEG, Indeo, or YUV data.
   - Controls to manage brightness and contrast.
   - Play MPEG-1 audio/video files).
   - Play AVI files to an output video device (e.g., VCR or TV monitor).

o  Audio Control, a new utility to control volume and port selection for all
   audio devices.

o  Support for the new FullVideo Supreme PCI video input and output option
   for AlphaStation systems. (See the "FullVideo Supreme Video Capture and
   Output Option for AlphaStation Systems" article in this issue for a full
   description on the newest PCI product for AlphaStation workstations.)

o  Audio Compression Manager, supporting IMA ADPCM (Adaptive Delta Pulse
   Code Modulation) for audio compression and decompression.

