A key advantage in Digital's multimedia environment on Alpha workstations is
the performance and quality of software video playback. JPEG, MPEG-1, and
Indeo files may be decompressed and displayed on a workstation using the
power of the Alpha CPU with no extra hardware. Software video may be used
for areas such as video documentation, presentations, mail, data storage,
and video conferencing.

Today, Multimedia Services supports the following:

o  Motion JPEG compression and decompression
o  Intel Indeo R3.2 compression and decompression
o  Intel Indeo 3.1 decompression
o  MPEG-1 decompression

Decompression refers to decompressing and playing back a video file to the
workstation monitor. Compression refers to creating a compressed video data
file from raw video format (YUV 4:2:2).

Highly dependent on the performance of the processor, a 320 x 240 Motion
JPEG file can be displayed at up to 40 frames per second in sample code.
MPEG-1 and Indeo playbacks are faster. In addition, Digital's patented
AccuVideo rendering techniques significantly enhance the perceptual image
quality of the video. MPEG-1, JPEG, and Indeo files displayed with AlphaVCR
