LinkWorks Mass Store

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Optical storage becomes available for LinkWorks objects

o  Pre-fetch of optical images to magnetic cache

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

LinkWorks Mass Store (SPD 54.95) is software that makes the functionality of
the Document Administrator of DECimage software available for the storage of
LinkWorks objects. It can be used together with image data, to migrate
LinkWorks objects from magnetic to optical storage, and in special
applications with large files, such as CAD/CAM.

Document Administrator provides for storage on optical disc, including
automatic (transparent to the user) caching on magnetic disc. When optical
disk is used, OSMS/OSDS is required. It allows for the grouping of related
documents on the same disk through its container principle and for direct
access to its documents on a server through file redirection. Additional
LinkWorks object classes have been defined that provide the Document
Administrator storage functionality. Users who want to make use of Document
Administrator storage for their objects can do this for the object classes
derived from the special LinkWorks Mass Store classes. The additional object
classes are LinkWorks Mass Store Object and LinkWorks Mass Store Folder.

o  LinkWorks Mass Store Object -- Using the object class LinkWorks Mass
   Store Object, the object references and attributes are stored within
   LinkWorks software, and the object content is stored on a Document
   Administrator container. In contrast to "ordinary" LinkWorks objects,
   which are copied to the user's file space on each access, the content of
   LinkWorks Mass Store objects is always accessed on the server where it
   resides. This avoids time and resource-consuming copying of large
   documents.

   The object class LinkWorks Mass Store Object is an abstract object class
   derived from the LinkWorks system class ObjectWithoutDocument. Users can
   derive their own object class from this that will have the property of
   the object content stored on Document Administrator. This object class is
   not restricted to image documents, but can be used for any type of
   document for which the Document Administrator functionality is required.
   This is most useful for documents that occur in large volumes (so that
   use of optical storage is required), or that are large in size (so that
   the direct access of document contents is required). It is also useful
   for documents that are updated infrequently (so that storage on
   write-once optical disc is viable). Examples include image documents,
   Computer Output to Laser Disc (COLD), PostScript files generated from
   word processing files, CAD/CAM drawings, and sound recordings.

o  LinkWorks Mass Store Folder -- The LinkWorks Mass Store Folder is derived
   from the LinkWorks folder. It has the additional property of allowing all
   LinkWorks Mass Store objects contained in it to be pre-fetched from
   optical disc into a magnetic disc cache. The pre-fetch is a function that
   is performed asynchronously on the Document Administrator server where
   the documents reside. Pre-fetching is used to minimize the amount of
   optical disk loads and jukebox movements, thus reducing access times.
   Depending on system configuration, pre-fetching can be done automatically
   when opening a folder or by means of an explicit action on an open
   folder.

   A system administrator's tool (MIGRATEtool) comes with LinkWorks Mass
   Store to move data from magnetic to optical disc. The user can specify
   when and where the LinkWorks Mass Store document needs to be stored to
   optical storage space. "When" is based on an installable amount of time
   after the last update. "Where" (i.e., on which optical disc) is based on
   document or folder attributes, enabling the user to group documents with
   the same characteristics, or have them reside in the same folder on the
   same optical disk.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

