POLYCENTER Capacity Planner V3.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides capacity planning for a multi-platform networked client/server
   environment

o  Maintains systems and network performance to ensure availability and
   enable resource planning

o  Allows choice of a product or service to fulfill capacity planning needs

o  Uses a graphical modeling interface that supports dynamic "what-if"
   analysis

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The POLYCENTER Capacity Planner tool allows the system manager to define the
system's total workload in terms of manageable units, and then report
against that information. Workloads and groups of workloads are used in
model generation and can be reported against in the Capacity Planner reports
or graphics. Workloads can be defined according to users, images, UICs,
process name, account name, and process mode in the context of the
particular operating system.

BENEFITS

o  State-of-the-art modeling -- The POLYCENTER Capacity Planner includes a
   graphical modeling interface from which "what-if" analysis can be
   performed dynamically.

o  Supports the following network protocols
   - OSI/DECnet
   - TCP/IP
   - UDP/IP
   - IPX/SPX
   - LAT

o  Supports the following operating systems
   - OpenVMS VAX and Alpha
   - Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1)

o  Provides Motif user interface for ease of use -- System modeling and
   "what-if" scenario can be performed with one mouse click.

o  Reporting -- Summary or detail reports on various performance statistics,
   including resource utilization, response time, throughput, queue link,
   and service time. Performance information is available for each CPU, HSC,
   disk, channel, adapter, CI, or Ethernet bus or Token Ring for current and
   projected workloads or configurations. Performance data for extended LAN
   components including bridges, routers, and brouters is also available.

o  Data collection -- The POLYCENTER Capacity Planner utilizes data
   collected by the POLYCENTER Performance Solution Data Collectors for
   OpenVMS VAX and Alpha systems, the POLYCENTER Performance Monitor Data
   Collector for Digital UNIX systems, and the new built-in data collector
   on PATHWORKS V5.0c.

POLYCENTER Capacity Planner allows users to make educated strategic
decisions in their IT environments. Whether the user is moving to a
client/server computing environment, downsizing, upsizing, or right-sizing,
capacity planning can act as a change management vehicle for their IT
systems as it plans system resource requirements from today's current state
to tomorrow's future needs.

