o  Support for mixed architecture clusters with OpenVMS VAX V6.1 and OpenVMS
   Alpha V6.1; and migration support for OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2 to OpenVMS VAX
   V6.1 and OpenVMS Alpha V6.1.

o  Support for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha V6.1 in the VMScluster system,
   including support for HSJ30 and HSJ40 controllers, each with HS Operating
   Firmware V1.5J or later; and the HSD30 controller with the HS Operating
   Firmware V1.5D or later. The latest remedial kit for Volume Shadowing
   software, VAXSHAD04_061 or AXPSHAD04_061, must be installed.

o  Support for Digital's VAX 4xxx, DEC 4xxx, AlphaServer 2100 departmental
   systems, and DEC 7xxx and DEC 10xxx datacenter class systems.

o  Support for the DECswitch 900EF Ethernet to FDDI switch (formerly the
   DECbridge 900MX).

BENEFITS

o  Designed, tested, and configured for disaster tolerance -- The
   configuration(s) and components supported in a Business Recovery Server
   FDDI or T3 VMScluster disaster-tolerant platform ensure optimal
   performance, component integrity, and system dependability. The
   Operations Management Station integration software provides the system
   and network management framework necessary for the rapid recovery of
   business-critical computing resources at the operational site.

o  Reduces impact of IT personnel changes -- Digital's Business Recovery
   Server V1.3 is a cost-effective disaster-tolerant solution that allows
   users to focus on their business goals versus systems availability.

o  Operations management of the entire configuration from either of two
   supported sites -- The Operations Management Station software ensures
   that a consistent disaster management process exists at each site.
