DECprint Supervisor for Xerox Printers for OpenVMS Alpha

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Easy integration of Xerox printers into OpenVMS Alpha environment using
   Digital developed print symbiont

o  Jointly engineered solution from Xerox and Digital

o  Communicates via Xerox's Dynamic Document Interface, a high speed,
   bi-directional SCSI shared disk interface

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECprint Supervisor for Xerox Printers for OpenVMS Alpha systems (SPD 54.54)
provides Digital supported software and hardware connectivity for Xerox
production printers. It allows one or more Xerox Model 4250, 4850, 4090,
4890, 4135, or 4635 Laser Printing Systems (LPS) to be attached to an
OpenVMS Alpha based system using Xerox's Dynamic Document Interface (DDI).
DECprint Supervisor for Xerox Printers software and the Xerox printer
communicate via a shared disk, leaving messages and print jobs on the disk,
which provides an extremely high bandwidth connection to the printer. This
solution is ideally suited for processing high volume, highlight color, and
critical print jobs such as reports, bills, or insurance policies.

The software supports typical Xerox printer data streams of ASCII text,
Metacode, and Image files. The symbiont provides typical OpenVMS printing
and queuing features, such as forms definition, setup modules, selection of
data types, and print orientation (portrait or landscape). All of the
standard OpenVMS print commands (Print, Define/Form, Init/Queue,
Start/Queue, Stop/Queue, Set, and Show Queue) are available to the user or
system manager. This software does not support PostScript, PCL, ReGIS, or
DDIF data streams.

All of the features of the supported printers also are available to the
user, such as highlight color, stapling, duplex, and offset stacking. A
user's print job may take advantage of the various Xerox printer data
streams, such as DJDEs, Metacode, and Image files. Print jobs may access
printer resources, such as fonts, signatures, logos, and forms.

DECprint Supervisor for Xerox Printers also provides a Management and
Diagnostic (MaD) utility for operator control of the print system and to
diagnose problems in communications between OpenVMS Alpha systems and the
Xerox printer. Printer resources are manageable in the OpenVMS environment.
A user on the OpenVMS Alpha system also may create DJDEs and then download
them in the printer.

BENEFITS

o  Digital software support is provided for Xerox printers.

o  Through the Xerox DDI, DECprint Supervisor for Xerox Printers is able to
   drive the Xerox printer at rated speed so that the user gets maximum
   return from the Alpha system and printer investment.

o  This fully integrated solution provides lower cost, higher functionality,
   and higher performance, eliminating the requirement for third party
   connection solutions.

o  There is a single point of contact for service. The user may place a
   service call to either Xerox or Digital, based upon user preference or on
   their determination of where the problem exists. The service organization
   called owns the responsibility for problem resolution and escalation.
   Each company still maintains its own products, but the user deals with
   one contact. Digital can dispatch Xerox field service and Xerox can
   dispatch Digital field service.

o  Xerox printer resources can be developed on the OpenVMS Alpha system,
   which provides better text editors and tools than working at the
   printer's console.

o  Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) systems can get access to the
   Xerox print system when the OpenVMS Alpha system is running UCX. Users
   moving their mainframe applications to Digital UNIX platforms have high
   speed printer access through the lpr/lpd interface of UCX.

o  Supported Xerox datastreams will print at rated speed on the printer.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

