POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS

HIGHLIGHTS

o  I/O performance improved with new offline utility to defragment the
   volume index file, INDEXF.SYS

o  Easier to use with enhanced GUI, keyboard mapping, and improved monitor

o  "Defrag PLUS" mode now uses RMS (Record Management Services) for improved
   performance and eliminates dependency on Oracle Rdb software

o  New tier pricing provides affordable small system solution

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS systems is a layered software
product that reduces file fragmentation through scheduled defragmentation
jobs. Digital's solution for file fragmentation offers the highest possible
data integrity. The POLYCENTER File Optimizer also provides a file placement
capability that allows the system administrator to place files on disk in an
order that optimizes the performance of the most frequently accessed files.
Users are continuing to experience tremendous growth in the amount of data
they need to manage on drives. The OpenVMS file system uses available disk
space efficiently, causing files to be fragmented as they are written to
nearly full disks. System performance can be negatively impacted by
fragmented files, so users need a tool that assures data integrity and
reduces file fragmentation to obtain and maintain optimal disk performance.

The volume index file, INDEXF.SYS, can become fragmented, slowing down
operations for all users. Often, when the INDEX.SYS becomes fragmented,
normal online defraggers cannot safely defragment this file. A new
capability in V2.1 allows users to defragment the volume index file with a
new offline utility. Note, however, that POLYCENTER V2.1 supports offline
defragmentation of INDEXF.SYS only on the "root" volume of a volume set (see
SPD 36.21 for details).

POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 for OpenVMS systems makes it easier for users
to establish and manage their defragmentation processes through an enhanced
graphical user interface (GUI). The enhanced user interface provides more
lists to ease defragmentation selection criteria, a keyboard mapping utility
that allows operators to assign functions to keys as well as the mouse, and
enhancements to the monitor window, allowing the POLYCENTER File Optimizer
to dynamically locate files according to user specified criteria.

POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 uses an RMS database to store policy and
configuration information, eliminating the need for an Oracle Rdb Runtime
License to defragment OpenVMS systems. In configurations tested to date, RMS
increased performance and did not affect functionality.

POLYCENTER File Optimize V2.1 protects your investment by maintaining all
the V2.0 features, including support for VAX and Alpha systems, hot file
placement, and unsurpassed data protection.

BENEFITS

o  Data integrity -- Ensures absolute data integrity through the use of the
   OpenVMS MOVEFILE primitive, which allows the safe movement of files on a
   disk.

o  Enhanced system management productivity -- Provides "set and forget"
   policy (once set, function occurs automatically) and automated,
   event-based scheduling, thus reducing the amount of time spent on these
   activities. An enhanced user interface reduces the probability of
   operations errors and the time it takes to do many operations.

o  Reduced backup and operator time -- Defragmentation of files improves the
   performance of backup operations; using this product requires less
   operator time and system resources.

o  Better performing disks -- Defragmentation of files improves application
   response time and allows higher disk utilization. The new offline
   defragmentation utility for INDEXF.SYS provides a safe way to streamline
   file location operations.

o  Need for an Oracle Rdb Runtime License eliminated -- Allows users without
   Oracle Rdb software to take advantage of the powerful POLYCENTER File
   Optimizer V2.1 capabilities.

o  New tiered pricing -- Makes V2.1 more affordable than ever to a broader
   range of users; the new pricing is especially attractive for users of
   desktop and workgroup solutions.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The POLYCENTER File Optimizer V2.1 will be available in May through Digital
and its business partners.

