   other applications

o  Includes preview release of POLYCENTER Archive/Backup for OpenVMS VAX
   systems, featuring graphical user interface and easier configuration

o  New tier pricing makes Storage Library System more attractive for entry
   level solutions

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Storage Library System V2.5 (SPD 29.67.10) continues the tradition of
providing the most automated backup solution on OpenVMS platforms. V2.5
incorporates Media Device Management Services for OpenVMS systems. This
common media management facility has been incorporated to provide more
responsive support of new devices and to allow media and device sharing
between multiple storage management applications. Other applications capable
of sharing devices through Media Device Management Services include
POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem V1.0 and POLYCENTER Hierarchical
Storage Management for OpenVMS V1.1. Through Media Device Management
Services, Storage Library System now provides support for a broader range of
loaders and libraries, including the TL820.

Storage Library System continues to offer the full range of capabilities,
including remote backup, unattended backup, user level restore through
online catalogs of backed-up and archived files, sophisticated media
lifecycle management, and automatic failure recovery in OpenVMScluster
environments.

Storage Library System users who purchase new version support receive
POLYCENTER Archive/Backup software as a free upgrade to Storage Library
System licenses.

The next major release of Digital's OpenVMS archive and backup product will
be V3.0. This version will include new features (a graphical user interface
and easier configuration) and will have a new name -- POLYCENTER
Archive/Backup for OpenVMS systems. A preview release version of POLYCENTER
Archive/Backup for OpenVMS VAX systems is included in the Storage Library
System V2.5 kit. These capabilities can be utilized with the existing
Storage Library license and are suitable for production use by new users.

The full release of POLYCENTER Archive/Backup for OpenVMS systems, planned
for the summer of 1995, will include tools to automatically upgrade users
from Storage Library System V2.5.

For more information, please see the "Storage Library System V2.4a for
OpenVMS VAX and AXP" article in the December 1994 issue of Digital's
Customer Update.

BENEFITS

OpenVMS users needing the capabilites of high capacity loaders and libraries
can now share these between storage management applications that utilize
Media Device Management Services, and can also take advantage of the
existing Storage Library System capabilities:

o  "Set and Forget" policies and support for unattended operations -- Saves
   system management time and expense.

o  User-based file restoration -- Improves user productivity and lowers
   system management costs.

o  Backups occur automatically per policy and copies of vital corporate data
   are maintained -- Increases data integrity and security.

o  Media Device Management Services -- Provides broader and shared device
   support, including the TL820.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Storage Library System V2.5, including the preview release version of
POLYCENTER Archive/Backup software, is available now through Digital and its
business partners. Media and documentation kits are purchased separately.

